# Gates that must distinguish clean, findings, and inconclusive.
#
# check-gates-are-honest.sh drives every gate listed here against three fixtures
# and requires it to be distinguished across all three: exit 0 on a clean
# subject, exit 1 on one with a real problem, exit 2 on one it cannot look at.
#
#   <subject-kind> <invocation> <argv…>
#
# invocation: path      -> the fixture is appended as the last argument
#             cwd       -> the gate runs with its working directory set to it
#             relocated -> the gate is COPIED into the fixture and run from there
#
# These two gates resolve their own repository from Path(__file__).parent.parent,
# so `relocated` is the only mode that works for them. Given a path they would
# ignore it, audit the real repository, and answer 0 -- a clean verdict about a
# tree they never looked at.
#
# The subject kind selects a fixture builder, and a kind with no builder is a
# finding rather than something to skip. Adding a gate means choosing one, which
# means answering "what does this look at, and what does it look like when there
# is nothing?" -- the question that produces the bug this file exists to catch.
#
# Kinds available today:
#   git-tree       the gate audits a git work tree    (empty = nothing tracked)
#   workflow-dir   the gate audits .github/workflows  (empty = no workflows)
#   skill-tree     the gate audits a skills/ directory (empty = no SKILL.md)

# The entry point the wiring check inspects, and the CI command that must call
# it. This repository's CI already runs these gates individually, so the entry
# point is a script that collects them rather than a new Makefile target.
# runner: scripts/run-skill-gates.sh
# ci-entry: .github/workflows/gates.yml
# ci-command: ./scripts/run-skill-gates.sh

skill-tree  relocated  tools/verify_skill_frontmatter.py

# tools/verify_skill_roots.py is NOT registered, and its absence is deliberate.
# It names .opencode/skills, .claude/skills and .agents/skills; this repository
# ships from `skills/` and publishes a derived byte-identical copy at
# `plugins/elohim/skills/`, so none of its three roots exists here and it has no
# subject to audit. It now returns 2 saying exactly that, instead of "OK, no
# duplicated name across 0 project-local roots" -- which is the fix that landed
# with the zero-subject floors.
#
# Adding `skills` and `plugins/elohim/skills` to its PROJECT_ROOTS would make it
# report nine "duplicates" that are not duplicates: AGENTS.md, CONSTRAINTS.md,
# CONTRIBUTING.md and README.md all state that `plugins/` is derived, and
# `tools/sync_adapters.py --check` is the gate that keeps the two equal. A
# gate that can see nothing is not a gate; a gate pointed at a mirror reports
# fiction. It is run by matrix.yml against a committed fixture, where it does
# have a subject, and that is where its verdict belongs.
